       'Analyse in the order a court or ombudsman would: is the loss within the insuring clause; does an exclusion apply, and does the insurer bear the burden of showing it; is a write-back engaged; has a condition been breached and what does the wording say the consequence is; apply the proximate cause test where causes compete.',
       'Reach a position: accept, accept in part (which heads, which limits), decline, or reserve rights pending named investigations; state the clause for every element and the facts on which it depends.',
       'Draft the letter in the standard structure (facts, policy terms, analysis, position, reservation of rights, next steps and the complaints route the wording or the insurer\'s procedure names) in a tone that is firm, courteous and free of adjectives.',
